In her own words, the exam will be based on the starred case studies in your Case Study

6
00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:16.235
Booklet A.

7
00:00:16.235 --> 00:00:21.642
Her exam announcement says the exam cases are the ones marked in yellow and starred.

8
00:00:21.642 --> 00:00:26.855
The blue test cases, like lactation and Jack's hearing loss, are not in the exam.

9
00:00:26.855 --> 00:00:30.459
And in a later post she said the exam's multiple choice,

10
00:00:30.459 --> 00:00:35.222
matching and drop-down questions are those same case questions, converted.

11
00:00:35.222 --> 00:00:38.569
So if you can answer every case question in writing,

12
00:00:38.569 --> 00:00:41.143
you've covered the closed questions too.

13
00:00:41.593 --> 00:00:43.889
Ten cases, in booklet order.

14
00:00:43.889 --> 00:00:46.103
Case 2, lymph node removal.

15
00:00:46.103 --> 00:00:47.333
Case 3, asthma.

16
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:49.137
Case 4, panic attacks.

17
00:00:49.137 --> 00:00:50.531
Case 6, diabetes.

18
00:00:50.531 --> 00:00:52.908
Case 8, joints and arthritis.

19
00:00:52.908 --> 00:00:56.352
Case 9, neurotransmitters and Parkinson's.

20
00:00:56.352 --> 00:00:57.664
Case 10, stroke.

21
00:00:57.664 --> 00:00:59.222
Case 13, fertility.

22
