28
00:01:20.164 --> 00:01:23.131
and the answer is built from her module content.

29
00:01:23.131 --> 00:01:26.407
And because the yellow shading covers the whole case,

30
00:01:26.407 --> 00:01:30.053
the unstarred questions inside those cases are in here too.

31
00:01:30.053 --> 00:01:33.700
Her helpline says an unstarred question can still be asked.

32
00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.140
The exam itself.

33
00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:40.224
Wednesday the fourth of November, on campus, in the computer labs.

34
00:01:40.224 --> 00:01:45.051
It moved from the fifth: she said so in her lecture on the seventh of October.

35
00:01:45.051 --> 00:01:48.207
The time is still to be confirmed, so check Canvas,

36
00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:53.096
and be at your venue forty-five minutes to an hour early, with your student ID.

37
00:01:53.096 --> 00:01:55.015
It's two hours and ten minutes.

38
00:01:55.015 --> 00:01:57.180
Thirty-two questions, ninety marks,

39
00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.708
and about thirty-seven per cent of the marks are written.

40
00:02:00.708 --> 00:02:03.493
Half marks only exist in the written answers.

41
00:02:03.493 --> 00:02:07.329
The multiple choice and matching questions are all or nothing.

42
00:02:07.779 --> 00:02:09.427
Two things she has promised.

43
00:02:09.427 --> 00:02:13.960
The diagrams in the case booklet will be in the exam: the joint, the synapse,

44
00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.726
the cerebrum, the cycle graph.

45
00:02:15.726 --> 00:02:18.786
The labels might change, numbers instead of letters,

46
00:02:18.786 --> 00:02:21.258
but the pictures are the ones you've seen.

47
00:02:21.258 --> 00:02:24.790
And she marks written answers at about half a mark per fact.

48
00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:28.793
So a four-mark question wants about eight short facts, one per line.

49
00:02:29.243 --> 00:02:30.578
How every track works.

50
00:02:30.578 --> 00:02:34.888
The examiner's voice reads the case, then each question with its marks.

51
00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:39.623
Then you hear her answer, line by line, with any tip she gave in her sessions.

52
00:02:39.623 --> 00:02:44.600
Each track ends with the whole thing once more, in one breath, and the last track,

53
00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.150
Rapid-fire, strings all of those together.

54
00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:51.581
Loop a track until the answer comes out of you before it comes out of me.

55
00:02:51.581 --> 00:02:53.038
Let's start with case 2.
